WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.360
It’s fun to bash pale, stale, middle
class males for being entitled AF.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.000
Especially when
they make it so easy.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.080
But privilege is complicated.
It’s not just black and white.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.280
Take the current batch
of Conservative MPs -

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.840
a bunch of white men so posh

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.720
they make Jeeves and Wooster
look like Kevin and Perry,

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.360
so privileged that
“the house of commons”

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:30.080
is how they describe literally
everyone else’s house.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.240
But whoever you are,
if you’re watching this, it’s 100%

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:36.800
that you’re packing
some kind of privilege.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.000
And just like a carry-on
containing oversize liquids,

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.720
you’ve got to check it.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.200
Take me. On paper,
I’m a triple-threat minority -

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:47.960
a black queer woman
living in post-Brexit Britain.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.360
I get to experience sexism,
mmm, racism, delicious,

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:55.600
or possibly the sexy blend
that is misogynoir.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.480
Get you a bigot who can do both.

00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.440
Plus, nobody really trusts bisexuals,

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:02.360
so I get straight up original
homophobia from straight people,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.440
biphobia from the queer community,

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.960
and a whole lot of well-meaning
confusion from my mum.

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.440
Oh, my mum?

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.720
Did I mention that she’s
a first-generation immigrant

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.000
and that I come from
a single-parent family?

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:16.520
World’s tiniest violin solo.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:21.520
OK, I’m not actually
going to shrug it off

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:23.360
and pretend that all
that stuff isn’t deep.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:25.240
I’ve been assaulted,
abused in the street,

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.440
and had it assumed
by strangers straight off the bat

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.200
that I must love chicken
and twerking.

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.800
Which is awkward because…

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.600
Love a bit of jerk and twerk.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.080
But, unlike a lot of people,

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.360
including some black queer women,

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.400
I have got a whole lot of privilege
going for me too.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:52.280
I’m cis,

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:55.680
meaning my gender identity matches up
with the one I was assigned at birth,

00:01:56.080 --> 00:01:56.880
neurotypical,

00:01:56.960 --> 00:02:00.320
which means my brain basically
works the way doctors expect it to,

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.640
able-bodied, I speak English,

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.720
and through being born in London
I bagged a British passport,

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:09.600
which is basically a golden ticket to
gain entry to the rest of the globe.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.600
A lot of why I’m doing OK today

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.160
is because I got lucky
in the lottery of life.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.720
People are really good at seeing
other people’s privilege,

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:20.400
but tend to be pretty bad
at seeing their own.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.160
It’s always my poshest friends
who say things like:

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:27.440
“Talking about money is so vulgar.
Let’s just all split the bill.”

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.520
I had tap water and a salad
for a reason, Florence.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.040
I’ll split the bill when you
chip in to heat my house.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.440
Also calling one quality a privilege
does kind of make it sound

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:39.080
like one end of the spectrum
is superior to the other.

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.480
You say black
like it’s a bad thing!

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:43.200
I love being black.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:45.280
I love having lips. I love seasoning.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.200
I love not being able to blush.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.920
It makes me so
mysterious, so enigmatic.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:53.000
Everyone’s asking: “What’s her
secret? What’s she hiding?

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:56.200
Maybe she’s born with it.
Maybe it’s melanin.”

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:00.360
We’ve got to stop using privilege
just as a stick to beat others with,

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.480
and start examining our own.

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:06.280
With great privilege,
comes great responsibility.

